    {
      "name": "DPP 07",
      "displayName": "DPP 07",
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "6910dd6ef03d970dedc21037",
          "question": "<p>In the reported figure, a capacitor is formed by placing a compound dielectric between the plates of parallel plate capacitor. The expression for the capacity of the said capacitor will be: \\((\\) Given area of plate \\(=A)\\)</p>\n<p><img title=\"56.PNG\" src=\"https://d2bps9p1kiy4ka.cloudfront.net/5b09189f7285894d9130ccd0/avuobggvz9stokuqor0r2hws2.PNG\" alt=\"\" width=\"215\" height=\"195\" /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><spantrebuchet ms=\"\" font-weight:normal=\"\" font-style:normal=\"\" text-align:center=\"\" data-sheets-root=\"1\">[JEE Main 2021, 27 Jul (Shift 1)]</spantrebuchet></p>",
          "image_url": "https://d2bps9p1kiy4ka.cloudfront.net/5b09189f7285894d9130ccd0/avuobggvz9stokuqor0r2hws2.PNG",
          "images": [
            "https://d2bps9p1kiy4ka.cloudfront.net/5b09189f7285894d9130ccd0/avuobggvz9stokuqor0r2hws2.PNG"
          ],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\(\\frac{15}{34} \\frac{K \\varepsilon_0 A}{d}\\)</p>",
            "<p>\\(\\frac{15}{6} \\frac{K \\varepsilon_0 A}{d}\\)</p>",
            "<p>\\(\\frac{25}{6} \\frac{K \\varepsilon_0 A}{d}\\)</p>",
            "<p>\\(\\frac{9}{6} \\frac{K \\varepsilon_0 A}{d}\\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 0,
          "explanation": "<p>(a) Capacitors, \\(C_1, C_2\\) and \\(C_3\\) are in series therefore,<br />\\[<br />\\begin{aligned}<br />&amp; \\frac{1}{C_{\\text {eq }}}=\\frac{1}{C_1}+\\frac{1}{C_2}+\\frac{1}{C_3} \\\\<br />&amp; \\frac{1}{C_{\\text {eq }}}=\\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{k A \\varepsilon_0}{d}\\right)}+\\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{3 k A \\varepsilon_0}{2 d}\\right)}+\\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{5 k A \\varepsilon_0}{3 d}\\right)} \\\\<br />&amp; \\frac{1}{C_{\\text {eq }}}=\\frac{d}{k A \\varepsilon_0}+\\frac{2 d}{3 k A \\varepsilon_0}+\\frac{3 d}{5 k A \\varepsilon_0} \\\\<br />&amp; \\frac{1}{C_{\\text {eq }}}=\\frac{(15+10+9) d}{15 k A \\varepsilon_0} \\\\<br />&amp; C_{\\text {eq }}=\\frac{15 kA \\varepsilon_0}{34 d}<br />\\end{aligned}<br />\\]</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "6910dd6ef03d970dedc21062",
          "question": "<p>A parallel plate capacitor with air as the dielectric has capacitance \\( C \\). A slab of dielectric constant \\( k \\) and having the same thickness as the separation between the plates is introduced so as to fill one-fourth of the capacitor as shown in the figure. The new capacitance will be -</p>\n<p><img title=\"q007.png\" src=\"https://d2bps9p1kiy4ka.cloudfront.net/5b09189f7285894d9130ccd0/54ma0a8of16utfc9w2udjxx2u.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"245\" height=\"73\" /></p>",
          "image_url": "https://d2bps9p1kiy4ka.cloudfront.net/5b09189f7285894d9130ccd0/54ma0a8of16utfc9w2udjxx2u.png",
          "images": [
            "https://d2bps9p1kiy4ka.cloudfront.net/5b09189f7285894d9130ccd0/54ma0a8of16utfc9w2udjxx2u.png"
          ],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\( (k+3) \\frac{C}{4} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( (k+2) \\frac{C}{4} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( (k+1) \\frac{C}{4} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{k C}{4} \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "6910dd6ef03d970dedc2105c",
          "question": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In the figure given below, four capacitors are shown with their respective capacities and the potential difference applied. The charge and the potential difference across the \\( 4 \\mu \\mathrm{F} \\) capacitor will be</p>\n<p><img title=\"asd.png\" src=\"https://d2bps9p1kiy4ka.cloudfront.net/5b09189f7285894d9130ccd0/6bf42t4yg5defidtcxgvc5eqi.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"230\" height=\"138\" /></p>",
          "image_url": "https://d2bps9p1kiy4ka.cloudfront.net/5b09189f7285894d9130ccd0/6bf42t4yg5defidtcxgvc5eqi.png",
          "images": [
            "https://d2bps9p1kiy4ka.cloudfront.net/5b09189f7285894d9130ccd0/6bf42t4yg5defidtcxgvc5eqi.png"
          ],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>600 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&mu;</mi></math>C, 150 volts</p>",
            "<p>\\( 300 \\mu \\mathrm{C}, 75 \\) volts</p>",
            "<p>800<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&mu;</mi></math>C, 200 volts</p>",
            "<p>580<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&mu;</mi></math>C, 145 volts</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 3,
          "explanation": "<p><em>Q</em> = <em>CV</em></p>\n<p><em><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>20</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mtext>&thinsp;</mtext><mo>&times;</mo><mn>300</mn><mtext>&thinsp;</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>&thinsp;</mtext><mn>1161</mn><mtext>&thinsp;</mtext><mi>&mu;</mi><mi>C</mi></math></em></p>\n<p>Charge through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>&mu;</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1161</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>580</mn><mtext>&thinsp;</mtext><mi>&mu;</mi><mi>C</mi></math></p>\n<p>Potential difference across</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>&mu;</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>580</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>145</mn><mi>V</mi></math></p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "6910dd6ef03d970dedc2106a",
